      "text": "<think>\nTo find the product of 606 and 797, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition. This means we can break down the multiplication into smaller parts and then add the results together.\n\nFirst, let's express 606 and 797 as sums of their digits:\n\n606 = 600 + 6\n797 = 700 + 90 + 7\n\nNow, we can use the distributive property to multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number:\n\n(600 + 6) * (700 + 90 + 7) = (600 * 700) + (600 * 90) + (600 * 7) + (6 * 700) + (6 * 90) + (6 * 7)\n\nNext, we can calculate each of these products:\n\n(600 * 700) = 420,000\n(600 * 90) = 54,000\n(600 * 7) = 4,200\n(6 * 700) = 4,200\n(6 * 90) = 540\n(6 * 7) = 42\n\nFinally, we add all these products together:\n\n420,000 + 54,000 + 4,200 + 4,200 + 540 + 42 = 482,982\n\nSo, the product of 606 and 797 is 482,982.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe product of 606 and 797 is \\boxed{482982}.\n</answer>",
