      "text": "<think>\nTo find the product of 192 and 927, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's how we do it step by step:\n\n1. **Write down the numbers one below the other, aligning them by their place values:**\n   ```\n     192\n   x 927\n   ```\n\n2. **Multiply 192 by the units digit of 927 (which is 7):**\n   - Multiply 192 by 7:\n     ```\n     192\n   x   7\n   ----\n     1344\n     ```\n   - Write this result below the line, aligning it with the units place.\n\n3. **Multiply 192 by the tens digit of 927 (which is 2):**\n   - Multiply 192 by 2:\n     ```\n     192\n   x   2\n   ----\n     384\n     ```\n   - Since we are multiplying by a tens digit, we need to shift this result one place to the left (because multiplying by 10 moves the digits one place to the left):\n     ```\n     192\n   x   2\n   ----\n     3840\n     ```\n   - Write this result below the previous one, aligning it with the tens place.\n\n4. **Multiply 192 by the hundreds digit of 927 (which is 9):**\n   - Multiply 192 by 9:\n     ```\n     192\n   x   9\n   ----\n     1728\n     ```\n   - Since we are multiplying by a hundreds digit, we need to shift this result two places to the left (because multiplying by 100 moves the digits two places to the left):\n     ```\n     192\n   x   9\n   ----\n     172800\n     ```\n   - Write this result below the previous one, aligning it with the hundreds place.\n\n5. **Add all the results together:**\n   ```\n     1344\n   + 3840\n   +172800\n   ------\n     176944\n   ```\n\nSo, the product of 192 and 927 is \\boxed{176944}. This is the final answer.\n</think>\n<answer>\n176944\n</answer>",
